From: ChopGimp <mathieu.redon@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] tile-backend-buffer: don't dup damaged mipmap tiles

When an operation copies its input (gegl_operation_context_dup_input_maybe_copy)
and then samples it at a mipmap level > 0 from several worker threads (e.g.
gegl:translate with a fractional offset while GIMP renders a layer group's
projection zoomed out), the source buffer can hand out a level > 0 tile whose
damage mask is still set. gegl_tile_dup() warns about it and the clone shares
data that is about to be regenerated, which leads to heap corruption
("double free or corruption").

Treat such a tile as missing: return NULL, so the zoom handler of the copy
rebuilds it from the level below, exactly like an uncached tile.
---
 gegl/buffer/gegl-tile-backend-buffer.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gegl/buffer/gegl-tile-backend-buffer.c b/gegl/buffer/gegl-tile-backend-buffer.c
--- a/gegl/buffer/gegl-tile-backend-buffer.c
+++ b/gegl/buffer/gegl-tile-backend-buffer.c
@@ -235,6 +235,15 @@ gegl_tile_backend_buffer_get_tile (GeglTileBackendBuffer *tile_backend_buffer,
 
   if (G_LIKELY(src_tile))
     {
+      /* a damaged (stale) mipmap tile, or one being rendered by another
+       * thread, must not be shared: let our zoom handler rebuild it.
+       */
+      if (z > 0 && (src_tile->damage || src_tile->lock_count))
+        {
+          gegl_tile_unref (src_tile);
+          return NULL;
+        }
+
       tile = gegl_tile_dup (src_tile);
 
       gegl_tile_unref (src_tile);
